Seasonal naive coincides with naive at every horizon that is a multiple of the season length ({{m.grid.season_length}}), so those two rows are identical by construction. The multivariate, univariate and placebo rows are separate skills against naive, not paired differences, and carry no interval here. The context rows use the context lengths of the grid, and the placebo row is computed on the {{a.lb.timesfm3_multivariate_placebo.identity.postrue.c512.naive.h28.n}}-card placebo panel (seed {{m.grid.placebo_seed}}), not on the full pool, so it is not directly comparable with the other rows. The log1p variant against naive has a cluster interval of {{a.secondary.log1p_vs_naive.h28.median.ci}} (median) at h = {{m.grid.h_primary_1}} and {{a.secondary.log1p_vs_naive.h56.median.ci}} at h = {{m.grid.h_primary_2}}. TimesFM-2.5 is compared with TimesFM-3 as a model comparison only: no TimesFM-2.5 cutoff is sourced, so it is never a cutoff control.

**Per-card Diebold-Mariano tests (secondary).** For the primary cell against naive, each comparison family has {{a.sig.timesfm3_univariate.identity.postrue.c512.naive.h28.family_size}} card-by-horizon tests. Rejections of equal accuracy (two-sided, no direction implied): at h = {{m.grid.h_primary_1}}, {{a.sig.timesfm3_univariate.identity.postrue.c512.naive.h28.bh_rejections}} by Benjamini-Hochberg (primary) and {{a.sig.timesfm3_univariate.identity.postrue.c512.naive.h28.by_rejections}} by Benjamini-Yekutieli (sensitivity); at h = {{m.grid.h_primary_2}}, {{a.sig.timesfm3_univariate.identity.postrue.c512.naive.h56.bh_rejections}} and {{a.sig.timesfm3_univariate.identity.postrue.c512.naive.h56.by_rejections}}. These counts never override the aggregate intervals.

**Forward-fill sensitivity is uninformative.** The exports that forward-fill at most {{a.secondary.ffill0_vs_ffill3.h28.median.ffill_days}} and at most {{a.secondary.ffill1_vs_ffill3.h28.median.ffill_days}} days give a skill difference from the primary export of {{a.secondary.ffill0_vs_ffill3.h28.median.value}} (interval {{a.secondary.ffill0_vs_ffill3.h28.median.ci}}) and {{a.secondary.ffill1_vs_ffill3.h28.median.value}} (interval {{a.secondary.ffill1_vs_ffill3.h28.median.ci}}). That is not evidence of robustness: the only non-observed day is {{m.fetch.missing_date}}, the as-of day whose archive was unavailable ({{m.fetch.missing_count}} day), and it lies outside every context window, so the sensitivity cannot change any forecast.

