## 5. Experiment B: exploratory red-team appendix

Experiment B is an explicitly **exploratory red-team appendix**, not a result of the main claim. The frozen rule (shock day: absolute z-score at least {{m.events.z_threshold}} against a trailing window of {{m.events.trailing_window}} trading days; events within {{m.events.decluster_gap}} trading days merged; guard band between {{m.events.pre_end}} and {{m.events.post_start}} excluded) produced {{m.events.n_pre}} pre-cutoff and {{m.events.n_post}} post-cutoff events. **Promotion verdict: {{b.tfm3.rule.timesfm3_univariate.none.promotion.verdict}}.** Reasons recorded with the verdict: {{b.tfm3.rule.timesfm3_univariate.none.promotion.reasons}}.

The primary statistic is the difference, post minus pre, of the error-recovery lag of TimesFM-3 relative to naive (restricted mean, event-cluster bootstrap). Descriptive effects at the primary threshold:

